# Kernel config fragment: core dumps for systemd-coredump (development record #346, docs/LINUX-DESIGN.md 9). Both default to y
# (their prompts exist under CONFIG_EXPERT only, which rk3128.config sets) and the kernel's core_pattern sysctl (CONFIG_SYSCTL, y with
# PROC_FS) is what systemd-coredump's /usr/lib/sysctl.d/50-coredump.conf sets; they are named here so the build fails
# ("config symbol lost") if a base kernel ever turns one off. Merged after rk3128.config by scripts/linux-build.sh.
CONFIG_COREDUMP=y
CONFIG_ELF_CORE=y
